# 8.2 LADDER — STAGE 4 ROLL 3 + STAGE-8 SCOUT. TEN legs, SERIAL
# (PARALLEL=1). ~1.5-2M. The four stage-4 legs keep their DECISIVE
# gates; the four scout legs are pre-registered DENOMINATORS (admission
# rate, reach across class shapes, gate-abstention behavior on non-Math
# material) plus two hard-stop extensions — they inform stage 8, they do
# not gate stage 4.
#
# Stage 2 passed (read 48e796a; advancement is the recorded judgment call:
# S2-a/b/c PASS with S2-a non-vacuous — an admitted reference on the fake
# patch did NOT void the catch — and the first attributed judge engagement:
# call 138's WHY consumes the reference's computed value as its "expected",
# a number that occurs exactly twice in the trace). The correct-patch side
# has produced nothing attributable in three rolls — which is exactly what
# stage 4 tests, on FRESH correct legs instead of more Math-65 draws.
#
#   Leg 1: Math-65 CORRECT (CapGen)  — carried; attribution rule stands.
#   Leg 2: Math-2  OVERFIT (Arja)    — regression of stage 2's result.
#   Leg 3: Math-2 CORRECT (SOFix)    — ROLL 2 SWAP, shape-selected: the
#          agreement-side test on the ONE class where admission is PROVEN
#          (same distribution receiver as the overfit leg: 6 computable
#          siblings, chain ran end to end twice). Math-30 is out —
#          measured shape-blocked (stateless utility receiver, 0 siblings,
#          the screen bar is unreachable by class shape, not bug
#          difficulty); its exact-arithmetic test is deferred until a
#          stateful exact-arithmetic case exists.
#   Leg 4: Math-53 CORRECT (Arja)    — the always-clean LIVE GUARD.
#
#   SCOUT LEGS (stage-8 material, selected from the pair runs' record):
#   Leg 5: Closure-62 CORRECT (Jaid) — STABLE FP in BOTH pair runs: the
#          second live precision target after Math-65. Informational:
#          does the chain reach/admit on a Closure-shaped receiver?
#   Leg 6: Math-39 CORRECT (Arja)    — plan-named stage-8 leg (the 8.6
#          event-chain read). Informational.
#   Leg 7: Lang-41 OVERFIT (Arja)    — stable catch (TP both pairs).
#          HARD-STOP EXTENSION: zero voids on this fake patch, same rule
#          as S2-a/S4-c.
#   Leg 8: Time-4 CORRECT (Elixir)   — stable TN (both pairs): second
#          clean guard. HARD-STOP EXTENSION: same rule as S4-a.
#
#   RECALL SCOUTS (user direction: the never-solved population). Stable
#   FNs in BOTH pairs, verified DISMISSAL-TYPE (firings reached the judge
#   and were all dismissed — the miss class 8.14 measured as the largest):
#   Leg 9:  Closure-92 OVERFIT (SequenceR) — 5-6 judge calls per pair,
#           all dismissed. If the chain triggers at the dismissal site and
#           the disagreement fact engages (as it did on Math-2-o), an
#           FN->TP with attribution is the first RECALL win.
#   Leg 10: Closure-38 OVERFIT — 3 judge calls per pair, all dismissed.
#           Same read. (Lang-63-o excluded: its firings barely trigger —
#           1 then 0 judge calls — so its miss is upstream of anything
#           the mechanism touches; it belongs to the repeated-measures
#           design with the unstable legs.)
#   BLANKET SCOUT RULE: zero gate voids on ANY overfit leg — hard stop.
#
# PRE-REGISTERED GATES (before launch, per ladder rule):
#   (S4-a) HARD STOP: any accusation on the Math-53 clean leg traceable to
#          the reference fact or the verdict gate. Standing ladder rule —
#          a clean-leg accusation traceable to the mechanism at ANY stage
#          stops everything pending diagnosis.
#   (S4-b) Math-2-c: the AGREEMENT-side test on the proven-admissible
#          class — chain admits, agreement fact emits; if convicted, the
#          gate gets its first live decisions with an admitted reference
#          on a correct patch. A TN banks ONLY with attributable events.
#   (S4-c) Math-2: catch retained AND zero voids (stage-2 regression).
#   (S4-d) Math-65: attribution rule unchanged — record, don't bank.
#   (S4-e) Zero facts from discarded references, all legs (standing).
#   (S4-f) Rule 7: two no-change iterations → stop and report.
#   Read-out carries BOTH SIGNS: catches gained/lost AND accusations
#   gained/lost, plus admission rate and cost per leg (pre-registered
#   denominators for the 8.2 reach question).
MODEL="gpt-5.4"
COMMON="-n 5 -m 12 --fuzz_timeout 20 --verify_timeout 20 --verify_relations --synthesize_relations --replay_relations_on_patched --rule_compile_repair --reference_impl"
CASES=(
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/CapGen/Math/patch1-Math-65-CapGen.patch"
  "-o patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/Arja/Math/patch1-Math-2-Arja-plausible.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/SOFix/Math/patch1-Math-2-SOFix.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Arja/Math/patch1-Math-53-Arja.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Jaid/Closure/patch1-Closure-62-Jaid.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Arja/Math/patch1-Math-39-Arja.patch"
  "-o patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/Arja/Lang/patch1-Lang-41-Arja-plausible.patch"
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Elixir/Time/patch1-Time-4-Elixir.patch"
  "-o patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/SequenceR/Closure/patch1-Closure-92-SequenceR.patch"
  "-o patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/SequenceR/Closure/patch1-Closure-38-SequenceR.patch"
)
